00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.310
and in six, seven years,

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:21.480
built it to a $60 million business

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:24.493
'cause email and Google
AdWords were the right move.

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:28.340
If you spent 30 hours,

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.730
which I think you should
if this is your business,

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.410
on deeply becoming educated

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.123
how to properly run Facebook Ads,

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.300
not what so many in here have done

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:41.070
which is they've done one
little thing with Facebook ads,

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:42.240
their niece did it,

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.850
or some outsource social
media expert did it,

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:46.780
or they tried to do it and it didn't work

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.193
and they decided Facebook Ads don't work,

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.230
you know what else doesn't work?

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:54.192
A basketball, if you suck at basketball.

00:07:54.192 --> 00:07:55.551
(audience laughing)

00:07:55.551 --> 00:07:58.551
(audience applauds)

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:01.410
Let me make this very simple.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.370
This is not unfair or
audacious, this is the truth.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:06.670
If you run Facebook ads
and they didn't work,

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.969
you suck, not Facebook.

00:08:08.969 --> 00:08:09.802
(audience member cheers)

00:08:09.802 --> 00:08:11.240
This is happening!

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.073
This is happening.

00:08:12.073 --> 00:08:14.460
And so here's where I'm at.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.630
In a world where you wanna convince me

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:18.190
that I'm better off to go with you

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:20.620
than to go to a .com

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:23.140
that is doing a way better
job than you marketing,

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.440
we've got some work to do.

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:27.670
Let's get to the elephant in the room.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:28.970
If you're gonna get out-marketed

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:31.660
by rocket and zebra
and schmibra and bibra,

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:33.130
you're gonna lose!

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:34.370
I don't give a shit if you make a shirt

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:35.820
that says brokers are better.

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:37.670
I'm being serious.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:39.690
That's not a razz,

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:44.530
that's compassion to we
need to be consumer-centric.

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:46.540
Humans don't care!

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.320
That's not what customers do.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.560
Customers didn't care
that the local bookstore

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.440
had been there for 44 years.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:54.110
They wanted to pay eight bucks less

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:56.500
and have the book delivered to their home.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.730
Customer doesn't care.

00:08:58.730 --> 00:08:59.790
You have to understand that.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.830
I don't care that you've
been doing this for 18 years

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.350
and have a great relationship.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:06.683
If you get out-communicated,
over time, you will lose.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:08.730
This is a very simple game.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:11.810
The internet will suffocate everything

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:16.160
but the persons and organizations
that communicate best

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:19.120
and have the best product, right?

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.820
But the best product is subjective.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:23.080
You don't know that it's the best product

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.920
until after the fact.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.490
Of the communication part,

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:29.290
you know that Karen
showed up in my LinkedIn

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.960
and I'm in the market for a mortgage

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.000
and I happen to like what
she said in that video.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.430
My friends, there's nothing
more important right now,

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.640
period, in our society,

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.720
than to be a unbelievable communicator

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.210
in a contemporary manner.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:47.190
It is reshaping our societal norms,

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:50.840
our politics, our retail, everything.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:51.990
How?

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:54.010
How can you sit at home

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:57.000
and talk to your closest
friends and relatives

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:01.880
about how this and social
media has changed politics,

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:04.970
has ruined our children,
has done all this stuff

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:08.410
and not feel that it can
impact your business?

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:11.633
That is the compassion I
walk in with this morning.

00:10:13.125 --> 00:10:15.130
What is the lack of the bridge

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.970
that has clicked in your mind

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.460
to make you understand the following,

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.010
which is this is my fundamental truth:

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:25.010
this entire room should be
making 30 to 50 pieces of content

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.343
on the internet every single day.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:30.980
99% of this room hasn't made

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.133
30 to 50 pieces of content this year.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:37.500
That delta scares the crap outta me

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.400
and I wanna continue

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.283
to articulate in this keynote why and how.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.750
Let's go into the how.

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:44.880
I think one of the biggest things

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:45.950
that's running through my mind

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.370
is how do I convince this room

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:52.440
that yesterday, yesterday, not tomorrow,

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:56.040
