00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.550
Now, what do you make your podcast?

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:18.000
As you guys can imagine,

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:22.080
no normal human being
thinks mortgage life is rad.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.810
(audience laughing)

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:26.610
We can agree with that.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:29.800
It's not the littiest thing in society.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.910
But what I do believe is the following:

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:37.100
I do believe that every
one of you has the ability

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:41.460
to start a podcast that
is a small business

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:45.370
or a community show
based on where you live.

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.330
The St. Louis Business
Podcast Business Podcast

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.440
is a real podcast

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.730
that anybody here could start,

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.330
and let me break this down to you

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:56.543
why I want to encourage so
many of you to start a podcast.

00:11:57.430 --> 00:12:01.240
I call it the high school party rule.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.750
I wanna take you back to high school.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:07.110
Now, think about sophomore,
junior, senior year,

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:10.660
and think very carefully
about that one kid

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.170
who wasn't the most popular kid in school

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.900
but had the great fortune

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.604
that his parents weren't
around on weekends.

00:12:17.604 --> 00:12:18.860
(audience laughing)

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:22.560
That kid, as a mid-level popular kid,

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:25.860
had the great idea of being
the person that threw the party

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:29.520
so the popular kids could
